{"id":"NCT06567743","title":"Phase 2 Study to Evaluate Safety and Efficacy of Cretostimogene Grenadenorepvec in High-Risk NMIBC","official":"A Phase 2, Multi-Arm, Multi-Cohort, Open-Label Study to Evaluate the Safety and Efficacy of Cretostimogene Grenadenorepvec in Participants With High-Risk Non-Muscle-Invasive Bladder Cancer (NMIBC)","summary":"This is a Phase 2, Multi-Arm, Multi-Cohort, Open-Label Study to Evaluate the Safety and Efficacy of Cretostimogene Grenadenorepvec in Participants with High-Risk Non-Muscle-Invasive Bladder Cancer.","conditions":["High-Risk Non-Muscle-Invasive Bladder Cancer"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Cretostimogene Grenadenorepvec"}],"criteria":"Cohort A Key Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Pathologically confirmed BCG-naïve high-risk high-grade NMIBC (i.e., CIS with or without Ta/T1 disease or high-grade Ta/T1 papillary-only disease without CIS) within 90 days of treatment allocation.\n* All visible disease must be resected, and all CIS resected or fulgurated, as feasible within 90 days prior to treatment allocation.\n* Acceptable baseline organ function.\n\nCohort B Key Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Pathologically confirmed BCG-exposed high-risk high-grade NMIBC (i.e., CIS with or without Ta/T1 disease or high-grade Ta/T1 papillary-only disease without CIS) within 90 days of treatment allocation.\n* All visible disease must be resected, and all CIS resected or fulgurated, as feasible within 90 days prior to treatment allocation.\n* Acceptable baseline organ function.\n\nCohort CX Inclusion Criteria\n\n* Pathologically confirmed high-risk high-grade BCG-unresponsive or BCG-exposed NMIBC (i.e., CIS with or without Ta/T1 disease or high-grade Ta/T1 papillary-only disease without CIS) within 90 days of treatment allocation.\n* All visible disease must be resected, and all CIS resected or fulgurated, as feasible within 90 days prior to treatment allocation.\n* Acceptable baseline organ function.\n\nKey Exclusion Criteria (Both Cohorts):\n\n* Current or past history of muscle-invasive, locally advanced or metastatic bladder cancer.\n* High-grade urothelial carcinoma in the upper urinary tract or prostatic urethra within 24 months or T2 in upper tract within 48 months or any history of locally advanced/ nodal or metastatic disease in the upper urinary tract.\n* Significant immunodeficiency.\n* Pregnant or breastfeeding.\n* Cohort CX Only: serial intravesical gemcitabine within 24 months","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":325,"start":"2024-09-16","pcd":"2027-03-31","upd":"2026-09-03","sponsor":"CG Oncology, Inc.","areas":["oncology"],"central":["Rebecca Tregunna, MD · 949 409-3700 · Rebecca.Tregunna@cgoncology.com","Pat Keegan, MD · 949 409-3700 · pat.keegan@cgoncology.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Banner MD Anderson Cancer Center","city":"Gilbert","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85234","s":"R","lat":33.3528,"lon":-111.789,"c":"Chinedu Mmeje, MD · 480-256-6444 · Chinedu.Mmeje@bannerhealth.com"},{"f":"Mayo Clinic Arizona","city":"Phoenix","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85054","s":"R","lat":33.4484,"lon":-112.074,"c":"Mark Tyson, MD · tyson.mark@mayo.edu"},{"f":"Arizona Urology Specialty","city":"Tucson","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85704","s":"STOP","lat":32.2217,"lon":-110.9265,"c":""},{"f":"University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences","city":"Little Rock","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72205","s":"R","lat":34.7465,"lon":-92.2896,"c":"Ahmet Aydin, MD · 501-526-5658 · maydin@uams.edu"},{"f":"Arkansas Urology","city":"Little Rock","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72211","s":"R","lat":34.7465,"lon":-92.2896,"c":"Jon Henderson, MD · 501-219-8900 · Jon@arkansasurology.com"},{"f":"Michael G Oefelein, MD Clinical Trials","city":"Bakersfield","pr":"California","zip":"93301","s":"R","lat":35.3733,"lon":-119.0187,"c":"Michael G Oefelein, MD · 661-310-1063"},{"f":"City of Hope","city":"Irvine","pr":"California","zip":"92518","s":"R","lat":33.6695,"lon":-117.8231,"c":"Cory Hugen